// smtp-gmail.ga — example of sending a real email to dadanhidyt@gmail.com
// through the official smtp extension, with TLS handled by a local stunnel
// tunnel (our extension speaks plain + AUTH LOGIN to localhost; stunnel
// encrypts to smtp.gmail.com:465 with certificate verification).
//
// ── Setup (one time) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 1. App password: Google Account → Security → 2-Step Verification →
//    App passwords (2FA must be enabled first).
// 2. TLS tunnel — write /etc/stunnel/gmail.conf:
//
//      foreground = yes
//
//      [gmail-smtps]
//      client = yes
//      accept = 127.0.0.1:2526
//      connect = smtp.gmail.com:465
//      verifyChain = yes
//      checkHost = smtp.gmail.com
//      sni = smtp.gmail.com
//      CAfile = /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt
//      setuid = stunnel4
//      setgid = stunnel4
//
//    then: apt install stunnel4 && systemctl enable --now stunnel@gmail
// 3. Extension: gar gne install smtp
// 4. Replace <APP_PASSWORD> below, then: gar run examples/smtp-gmail.ga
//
// ── Real test results (2026-10-09) ─────────────────────────────────
// • Direct delivery to the Gmail MX (port 25, no TLS/authentication):
//   the dialogue was accepted all the way through RCPT + DATA, then
//   REJECTED by Google policy:
//   550 5.7.26 "Gmail requires all senders to authenticate with either
//   SPF or DKIM."
// • The authenticated submission path above (TLS via stunnel + AUTH
//   LOGIN): accepted, 250 — the email landed in the inbox.
use "smtp"

$s = smtp.connect("127.0.0.1", 2526, 20000)
$s.auth("dadanhidyt@gmail.com", "<APP_PASSWORD>")
$s.from("dadanhidyt@gmail.com")
$s.to("dadanhidyt@gmail.com")
$s.subject("GaLang smtp extension test")
print("send  : " + str($s.send(
  "Hi!\n\n" +
  "Test email from the official GaLang smtp extension.\n" +
  "Path: use \"smtp\" → stunnel → smtp.gmail.com:465 (TLS).\n"
)))
print("close : " + str($s.close()))
